"""Compare velarx with podman on the same operations, measured by hyperfine.

    tools/perf-compare [--velarx BIN] [--podman BIN] [--out DIR] [options]
    tools/perf-compare --summarize DIR        (redo the table and graphs)

Both engines run rootless with the same OCI runtime (crun), the same
cgroup manager, the same events backend, and the same private registry
(a distribution `registry` on a port of its own, seeded with skopeo
registry to registry from the source images, so the Internet is not in
the timings).  Each engine has a store of its own under a scratch
directory (default /var/tmp/vxperf-XXXX, removed at the end): its own HOME,
XDG_* directories, --root, --runroot and --tmpdir (skopeo too runs with a
home of its own).  Nothing of the default stores or configuration of either
engine is read or written; podman is
only ever run with --root/--runroot/--tmpdir of the scratch directory, and
the script aborts when `podman info` reports other directories.

The operations (see BENCHMARKS): cold and warm pull of a small and of a big
image, run --rm of both (the run of the big one must equal the small one),
create+start+rm, ps -a, images, build of three RUN steps (cold with
--no-cache and cached), rm, rmi, inspect of an image and of a container,
and exec in a running container.  One hyperfine JSON per benchmark and
engine goes to OUT/json/NAME.ENGINE.json; OUT also gets summary.md (the
table on standard output too: mean +- sigma per engine and the ratio
velarx/podman, under 1.0 means velarx is faster), environment.txt, and the
graphs (SVG always, PNG with matplotlib when it is installed).

Needs: hyperfine, podman, crun, skopeo and `registry` (distribution) for a
private registry; or --registry HOST:PORT for one that already holds the
images as NAME:TAG (the last path component of the source images).  The
timings are noisy while the host is busy: the load average is recorded at
the start, between benchmarks and at the end, and a warning says when it is
above --load-warn.
"""

